      "writtenOn": "2023-04-21T07:42:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Note toLowerCase() is different from DNS case-insensitive definition\ne.g. \"RÉMI\".toLowerCase() is \"rémi\"\n\nBut https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6762#page-46 says that \"Accented characters are *not* defined to be automatically equivalent to their unaccented counterparts\". So the \"DNS lowercase\" here should be \"rÉmi\"\n\nSo basically: to calculate the \"DNS lowercase\" you look at each UTF-8 (or UTF-16 for Java) character; if they\u0027re in range 0x41 to 0x5A (A-Z) you add 0x20, so they\u0027re transformed into a-z. Otherwise they are kept as-is.\n\nYuyang has b/272194544 open where he\u0027d probably need to use such utils, so you can sync with him.\n\n(Yes I know, aosp/2474710 is wrong and needs to be fixed too !)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 49,
        "startChar": 48,
        "endLine": 49,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "1f85cd1d0637589f2fe46398801d690dc6b0a8bd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
